@Maggie Atkinson @Jeffrey Guerrero I agree with the points in the best practices (ty!), but with a request and a note, please:
1. For the Reco'd version, I think the body copy needs to have a narrower width so the block of text looks centered (while staying left aligned). Right now, it runs long and the eye has to bounce too widely between header to body to button. 
2. The body text in question isn't that long so I'd argue that the reading of it isn't too hard in this case. =) That being said, I agree with the Reco'd version if we can adjust width of body copy. CC @Brent Trotter
